          %p
            2) The map,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} mx
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mx_{A,B}: A \otimes B \to A \oplus B
          %p
            An
            %strong isomix category
            is a mix category in which the mix map is a natural isomorphism,
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo :
                    %mo ⊥
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo ⊤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m: \bot \simeq \top
          %p In an isomix category, the mixor is automatically a natural transformation. The mix map being an isomorphism does not imply that the mixor is a natural isomorphism.
          %p
            An isomix category in which the mixor is a natural isomorphism is a
            = succeed "." do
              %strong compact LDC
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊗
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes
            and the par
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊕
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \oplus
          %h3#starautonomous_category Star-autonomous category
          %p
            Any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-autonomous+category"} star-autonomous category
            has an underlying symmetric linearly distributive category where we define
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi B
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo *
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mo *
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\oplus B \coloneqq (A^* \otimes B^*)^*
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi B
                    %mo ≔
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mo *
                    %mo ⊸
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\oplus B \coloneqq A^* \multimap B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊸
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \multimap
            is the internal-hom. The left distributor, for instance, is obtained as follows:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:rowlines => "solid"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mrow
                            %mtable{:rowlines => "solid"}
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi A
                                  %mo ⊗
                                  %mi B
                                  %msup
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mo *
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi A
                                  %mo ⊗
                                  %mi B
                                  %msup
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mo *
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %mi A
                                  %mo ⊗
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi A
                                  %mo ⊗
                                  %mi B
                                  %msup
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mo *
